  "rationale": "Raids are live and this is a long-horizon sweep, so unlike balance-gate-v1 the movement here is the mechanic rather than a content hash. Inbound raids arrive on stream 10 and burn or carry off shelved grimoires, and every world draw after a raid keys on a shifted stepOrdinal, so grimoire counts fall by 36.6 (-4.19 SE) and instance counts with them. The new numbers are right because they are the first ones measured on a build where a universe can be attacked; the old ones describe a universe nothing could reach.",
